        "original_id": "8643e6ee-58e6-5e07-9994-8378694714f2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Horten brothers\n- Products: Horten H.XVIII, Horten Ho 229\n- Concepts: flying wing configuration, turbojet engines, stealth characteristics\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- During World War II, the Horten H.XVIII was a proposed German intercontinental bomber.\n- The Horten H.XVIII was designed by the Horten brothers.\n- The Horten H.XVIII featured a flying wing configuration, turbojet engines, and stealth characteristics.\n- In the 1940s, the Horten brothers designed some of the most revolutionary aircraft of the decade despite having little, if any, formal training in aeronautics or related fields.\n- In the 1940s, the Horten brothers designed the Horten Ho 229, which was the world's first jet-powered flying wing.",
